    <fields>
        <fullName>ASU_Geomarket_Code__c</fullName>
        <description>[??] - is maintained by import and defined by Admission Services.  It breaks ASU’s target market into more geographic areas (still several zipcodes but finer definition than what CollegeBoard assigns, AZ is broken into 10 or 11 AZ Geomarkets).</description>
        <externalId>false</externalId>
        <label>ASU Geomarket Code</label>
        <length>10</length>
        <required>false</required>
        <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
        <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
        <type>Text</type>
        <unique>false</unique>
    </fields>
    <fields>
        <fullName>ATP_Code__c</fullName>
        <description>[??] - American Testing Program (ATP) Code is a set of numbers used for standardized testing such as SAT and ACT. A CEEB code is a standardized ID number that is assigned to a high school, college, or university. CEEB codes are issued by the Educational Testing Service (ETS). These 4- to 6-digit codes are mostly used in college entrance exams such as the SAT and ACT.</description>
        <externalId>false</externalId>
        <inlineHelpText>American Testing Program (ATP) Code is a set of numbers used for standardized testing such as SAT and ACT. This field also represents the CEEB code by the Educational Testing Service.</inlineHelpText>
        <label>ATP Code</label>
        <length>6</length>
        <required>false</required>
        <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
        <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
        <type>Text</type>
        <unique>false</unique>
    </fields>
